open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":11,"created_at":"2026-06-19T08:14:39Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T07:53:58Z","closed_at":"2026-07-04T16:14:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n- Not reproducible in v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\nTested on a Motorola Edge 50 Pro - Android 16\n\n### System information\n\nMotorola Edge 50 Pro - Android 16 - W1UMS36H.52-73-8-1\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn mobile devices, touching a Button results in duplicated events thus running logic attached to the pressed signal twice. \n \nThis issues appeared after the introduction of [BaseButton: multitouch support\n#110893](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110893#issue-3453390367) as testing on 4.6.3 stable does not replicate the problem. \n\nThere should be only one event processed per press/touch\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project with a scene that contains a Control root node and a Button child\n- Attach a script to the root node\n- Connect the Button pressed signal to the root script and print a message in the body of the function\n- Run the project on a mobile device with the default Project Settings ('Emulate Mouse From Touch' enabled)\n- See a duplicated print in the Output Dock\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Button_duplicated_gui_event.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29129392/Button_duplicated_gui_event.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_